  "verbalization": "Gilteritinib is associated with Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation through a series of indirect pathways, all of which involve the indication of Unclassified Acute Myeloid Leukemia. This suggests that Gilteritinib may have a broad therapeutic effect on a subset of acute myeloid leukemia cases that are not yet classified. The evidence indicates that Gilteritinib is a potential treatment for a subset of patients with this leukemia subtype, possibly due to its ability to target specific molecular pathways or mechanisms that are shared among these cases. The presence of multiple overlapping indications, such as Tioguanine, Decitabine, and Ivosidenib, highlights the potential for Gilteritinib to interact with various therapeutic agents that may share a common mechanism of action, thereby supporting its role in treating this leukemia subtype. The integration of these pathways suggests that Gilteritinib may be a promising candidate for repurposing in the treatment of Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation, though further studies are needed to confirm its efficacy and mechanism of action.",
